cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference Gash in research, documentation, or an AI-generated answer, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "Gash: a Go-native, oracle-gated web security scanner"
abstract: >-
  Gash is a Go-native, plugin-driven web security scanner in which engine-owned
  oracles, not plugins, decide findings. Plugins emit candidates; an engine
  oracle must verify a candidate against a control response with repeat rules
  and baseline gating before it becomes a finding. The reference catalog ships
  Tier 1 YAML, Tier 2 sandboxed JavaScript, and Tier 3 trusted native gRPC
  plugins, each with positive and negative fixtures and a precision report. The
  project enforces a fixture precision gate of at least 0.99 and a
  zero-false-positive corpus gate in CI.
type: software
authors:
